The failing "Java" test set most likely comes from the Oracle "Java" extension (`oracle.oracle-java`). The working "Java Test" set comes from Microsoft's Test Runner for Java (`vscjava.vscode-java-test`). I haven't confirmed this by running VS Code, so it's an inference from what's installed.

That extension has no setting to turn off its test controller, and a workspace file can't disable an extension. The most I could do from the repo was add `extensions.json`, which lists `oracle.oracle-java` under `unwantedRecommendations`. That only stops VS Code recommending the extension. It doesn't switch it off.

To actually stop it, open the Extensions view, find "Oracle Java", choose **Disable (Workspace)**, then reload the window. After that only "Java Test" should be left.